{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/483486-totem-questions","id":483486,"title":"Totem questions.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-17T06:43:01-07:00","id":483486,"title":"Totem questions.","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> I'm newer to Werewolf in that I never played first edition, but I am currently running a second edition game.<br /> Having played Blood and Smoke (2E Requiem) I know that some of the information in the book probably assumes that I have a brief understanding of first edition Werewolf.<br /> <br /> My question: When a pack is in the world of the flesh, where is their totem? Does it follow them around somehow un-manifested? Can it talk to them? Can the pack see it and interact with it?<br /> If not, does the totem only come into play when the pack crosses over into the Hisil?<br /> <br /> When storytelling the totem in a game, how do you portray them? Does a player at the table role play them like they do the other members of the pack (Wolf Blooded, Human etc.)?<br /> <br /> So far I have run two sessions of our adventure and the totem hasn't been brought into play yet. Any advice would be greatly appreciated. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1310,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1310-samare","user":"Samare","date":".  Edit: added words 04-17-2015, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1310-samare","name":"Samare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1310_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T06:57:30-07:00","id":483513,"title":"","content":"Depends on the totem, I think. Their available manifestations will dictate how involved in the material realm they can be. <br /> <br /> That said, their pack automatically counts as resonant so they may want to follow them around as they are an easy supply of essence, plus it helps get a foothold on all the other tricks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T07:18:06-07:00","id":483521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/483486-totem-questions#post483486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello,<br /> <br /> I'm newer to Werewolf in that I never played first edition, but I am currently running a second edition game.<br /> Having played Blood and Smoke (2E Requiem) I know that some of the information in the book probably assumes that I have a brief understanding of first edition Werewolf.<br /> <br /> My question: When a pack is in the world of the flesh, where is their totem? Does it follow them around somehow un-manifested? Can it talk to them? Can the pack see it and interact with it?<br /> If not, does the totem only come into play when the pack crosses over into the Hisil?<br /> <br /> When storytelling the totem in a game, how do you portray them? Does a player at the table role play them like they do the other members of the pack (Wolf Blooded, Human etc.)?<br /> <br /> So far I have run two sessions of our adventure and the totem hasn't been brought into play yet. Any advice would be greatly appreciated. Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>If the pack have a locus or other crossing point between Flesh and Spirit under their control, then their totem can (if it wants) fairly easily cross between worlds to accompany the pack around.<br /> <br /> If accompanying the pack in the Flesh, the totem is likely to be in Twilight form (especially if it doesn't have the Materialise Manifestation). Werewolves can perceive Twilight spirits so will be able to see and talk with it just fine.<br /> <br /> For my games, I run the totems rather than having a player play them. I tend to run totems as being quite demanding and having specific expectations of their pack - for example, the pack totem for my Paris game, the spirit of a foundry, is aligned with the city spirit Court of light and didn't hesitate to express its displeasure at one of the pack members' darkness-Court spirit allies being present; it has required that the pack build braziers that must be kept lit in the Flesh and Spirit of their lair for it; and it got very pissed off when the pack blundered disorganisedly through a fight with some local lesser spirits, since it expects them to be organised, ordered and effective - when they fail or are defeated, that reflects badly on the totem, which has serious ambitions in terms of the local spirit politics.<br /> <br /> Currently the totem is still very weak so it spends most of its time guarding the Locus in the pack's lair; it does meddle extensively in the immediate vicinity, including suddenly Manifesting to chastise one of the (quite scared) human pack members for doing things that it doesn't like (throwing out some metal goods rather than reusing them, in this specific case), but once the pack have secured more of their territory and garnered it more power it will be more willing to accompany them around.<br /> <br /> Another pack totem I ran for a long 1e game, a spirit born of lightning and electricity, tended to scoot around with the pack everywhere in Twilight, and regularly would communicate with them via hijacking their phones, televisions or whatever to deliver its crackling, hissing messages from the beyond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}